{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792301858,"nonce":"KzXDV4LXgLIBBGnfa6HAWq7sfek=","message":"2026-10-18, two parts. (1) The atlas overflow that blanks the frame: root cause is blinc_abi's hl_blinc_tree_display_list, which cleared the atlases after every overflowing walk, the second too, and then returned that walk's records, which name glyphs in atlases that were now empty. Fixed in blinc_abi a92f5c0 (its issue 807fbba): the atlases are cleared between the walks only, and the last walk's records and polygon points stand; build_with_retry carries three unit tests. Verified end to end with a snapshot scene of SF Mono text at 32px (a dozen distinct glyphs fill the 4096 atlas) beside a small label in another font: with the current pin the whole frame is blank, with the fix the label draws and only the node that does not fit is left out. Not pushed or pinned yet: it goes on blinc_abi main and on its branch ashui (b483813), which ashui pins. (2) The glyphs that fill the atlas: blinc_text's rasterizer builds its swash scaler with hint(false), and swash then rasterizes CFF outlines in font units (hint true: 19x25 pixels; false: 1020x1503, digit 3 at 32px in SF Mono). Asked of blinc-16 (the Blinc session): hint(true) when the font data starts with OTTO, in both rasterize functions (rasterizer.rs lines 88 and 171 at Blinc 9ed1d29b). Until Blinc has it, SF Mono text still draws too large; ashui's component size gallery keeps its TrueType font stack.","files":null}]}